    "body": "# Description\n\nThe distributed `Linear` tests in `run_numerics.py` only use 2D inputs, so the sequence-parallel all-gathers never see the `[seq, micro-batch, hidden]` layout. #3720 shows what that misses. With the NVFP4 recipe, the 2.21.0 pre-release `d77ef88c` crashed in the backward all-gather of a row-parallel `Linear` with sequence parallelism when the micro-batch was 1, and the existing tests passed on it. #3628 later fixed the shape bookkeeping on main and on `release_v2.21`.\n\nThis PR adds a test for that layout. It is test-only.\n\nRelated: #3720, #3628\n\n## Type of change\n\n- [ ] Documentation change (change only to the documentation, either a fix or a new content)\n- [ ] Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\n- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)\n- [ ] Breaking change (fix or feature that would cause existing functionality to not work as expected)\n- [ ] Infra/Build change\n- [ ] Code refactoring\n\n## Changes\n\n- `tests/pytorch/distributed/run_numerics.py`: `test_linear_3d_input` runs a sequence-parallel `te.Linear`, column- and row-parallel, on `[seq, micro-batch, hidden]` inputs with micro-batch 1 and 3. The sequence has `WORLD_SIZE * SEQ_LEN` tokens, so every rank holds `SEQ_LEN` of them in the sequence-parallel layout. The test compares the output and the input gradient with a single-GPU `Linear`, using the existing helpers and tolerances. It runs for every recipe that `test_numerics.py` parametrizes.\n\n## Testing\n\nTwo B300 GPUs (sm_103), TE built for `103a`, torch 2.14.1+cu130, cuDNN 9.24:\n\n| TE | `test_linear_3d_input`, NVFP4 |\n|---|---|\n| `d77ef88c` (2.21.0 pre-release from #3720) | **fails**: row-parallel, micro-batch 1 in `swap_first_dims` (\"Input is not allocated\"); row-parallel, micro-batch 3 in `CheckScaleTensorShape` (`columnwise_scale_inv.shape == expected`). Both column-parallel cases pass, and so does the existing `test_linear`. |\n| `7457e47d` (`v2.21.0`, includes #3628) | passes |\n| main `63451d6b` | passes |\n\nOn main with this PR, `tests/pytorch/distributed/test_numerics.py` passes for all six parametrizations (None, fp8, mxfp8, fp8_cs, fp8_block_scaling, nvfp4): 6 passed. Black 24.4.2 with the repository's pre-commit options leaves the file unchanged.\n\n# Checklist:\n\n- [x] I have read and followed the [contributing guidelines](https://github.com/NVIDIA/TransformerEngine/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.rst)\n- [x] The functionality is complete\n- [x] I have commented my code, particularly in hard-to-understand areas\n- [ ] I have made corresponding changes to the documentation\n- [x] My changes generate no new warnings\n- [x] I have added tests that prove my fix is effective or that my feature works\n- [x] New and existing unit tests pass locally with my changes\n",
